You're one to talk!

20
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:00,880
We don't remember who you are either! Yo!

21
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:04,097
You do know that I was with y
'all from the jump, don't ya?

22
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:06,957
Sorry to say this, but I
can't say that I remember you.

23
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:07,870
Shut it!

24
00:01:07,953 --> 00:01:11,120
Nobody knows who your scrawny
ass is either! Yes you do!

25
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:12,977
I'm the one who just called
for help on the radio!

26
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:14,757
Maybe you only did that to trick us!

27
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:15,670
Wait a minute.

28
00:01:15,753 --> 00:01:17,217
You there with the black hair.

29
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:19,535
Why did your nose just start bleeding?

30
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:22,930
What the...?

31
00:01:23,013 --> 00:01:25,820
I couldn't see all that well, but Ermes,

32
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:30,786
when I punched the enemy's stand in the
face, one of these three stumbled a bit.

33
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:34,257
Get back right now!

34
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:35,920
Stay away from the water!

35
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:37,907
No, you've got it all wrong!

36
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,657
My nose is bleeding because that bitch
hit me in the face when she grabbed me!

37
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:42,570
See, look!

38
00:01:42,653 --> 00:01:43,541
Her bloody hand!

39
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:45,248
It's proof that she did it!

40
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,200
Are you for real?

41
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:51,657
I didn't hit her, my finger
just scraped her teeth!

42
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:55,564
I was most definitely here from
the start if anyone's the killer.

43
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,017
It's gotta be one of you.

44
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:00,677
Oh, yeah Remember what happened when
the chief was chatting with his Cutter?

45
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:04,557
You were over there talking mad shit
Ain't that right little miss bitch.

46
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:05,740
Yeah, that's true.

47
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:09,174
You know what the two of you
seem pretty suspicious, too

48
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:12,870
What

49
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:18,040
It's true, so the black hair did do it.

50
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:20,657
How the hell did you
figure out it was her?

51
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:24,680
Well, to tell the truth, I have
no idea if it actually was her.

52
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:28,078
That's why I'm just gonna
knock out all three of you!

53
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:33,940
You bitch!

54
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:36,260
Who the fuck do you think you are?

55
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:38,337
D-did she just...

56
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:39,920
Now my plan's ruined.

57
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:41,797
I wanted to kill you separately.

58
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:45,292
I was gonna get you into the
water and tear you to shreds.

59
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,577
But your little trick surprised me.

60
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:50,417
I really didn't think you could
get out of that situation,

61
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,857
but that threat power of
yours is a pain in the ass.

62
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:55,360
What the hell is going on with them?

63
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:57,497
It can't be all three of them, can it?

64
00:02:57,580 --> 00:02:58,897
This doesn't make any sense.

65
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:00,627
Who's the actual stand user?

66
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,120
Once again, you're wrong.

67
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:15,820
Stand powers are special.

68
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:19,240
Each individual only gets one.

69
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:22,937
The girls who were actually
here from the very beginning

70
00:03:23,020 --> 00:03:26,196
were the ones with the black
hair and the shaved head.

71
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:35,596
They decided to go near the tractors,

72
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:39,197
so I decided to kill them and take
over their bodies and intellect.

73
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:42,320
On the other hand, this body of mine is...

74
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:46,217
You need the body I
created from the scraps

75
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:49,006
of flesh left over from
the missing prisoners!

76
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:16,737
I have to hold my hand and hold my hand.

77
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:18,340
I'm going to turn around.

78
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:21,068
I'm going to trap and hate.

79
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:24,020
Okay, alright.

80
00:04:24,860 --> 00:04:27,737
I'm a survival day.

81
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:28,977
Get away from.

82
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:30,377
No more time.

83
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:32,057
I don't wanna say it.

84
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:33,097
No more time.

85
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:34,337
Let's go, go.

86
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,677
One, two, three.

87
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:37,117
Come and find a way.

88
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:38,297
Life for me.

89
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:41,340
I'm a my one.

90
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:30,896
That strange black goop is
coming out of their bodies.

91
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:34,860
My once divided body is now whole again.

92
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:39,117
If it is to protect the
power and memory that Pale

93
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:41,965
Snake's discs most
graciously bestowed upon me.

94
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:44,178
I am willing to do anything it takes

95
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:47,920
to repay the great debt I owe him.

96
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:52,257
It's my mission to get rid of anyone who
approaches the discs in the storehouse.

97
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:53,170
Damn it!

98
00:05:53,253 --> 00:05:55,757
Where the fuck is the
actual stand user hiding?

99
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,280
Think again, Ermes.

100
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,940
The user is...

101
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,860
the thing itself! Huh?

102
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,220
It's alive.

103
00:06:02,580 --> 00:06:06,100
See, this thing is a living
organism born in the water.

104
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:08,478
And from the discs, it gained power.

105
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:12,257
And the one guarding those discs
was never human to begin with.

106
00:06:12,340 --> 00:06:13,800
A living organism?

107
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:17,609
Are you talking about all those
tiny killer plankton things?

108
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:21,517
Since the storehouse doesn't
have a constant supply of water,

109
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:24,097
it's probably moving by
consuming water from the

110
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:27,077
bodies of its victims in
order to protect the discs.

111
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:29,740
It exists on land by multiplying itself.

112
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:31,017
But there's a catch.

113
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:34,717
Just like gas for a car, it needs to
replenish its water when it runs out.

114
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:37,537
If we want to get the disks
back from this creature,

115
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:42,077
we have to make sure it doesn't get close
to the water, and then defeat it quickly.

116
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,101
Hold up, Jolene.

117
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:48,281
Even if all that crap is true, how can that
walking parasite with a face talk to us?

118
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:49,920
I am F .F.

119
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:52,820
You will call me by my name or not at all!

120
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:58,560
A famous astronomer by the
name of Fred Hoyle once said,

121
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:03,280
It is wrong to assume, even
probabilistically speaking,

122
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:07,089
that living organisms were
spontaneously born on this Earth.

123
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:11,237
The power of intellect was already a
pre-existing force in this universe,

124
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:14,732
and it is that intellect which
created the origin of life.

125
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:19,297
To put it another way, it can be said
intellect preceded even the Big Bang,

126
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:24,300
and that all organisms in matter itself
already possess that intellect. Huh?

127
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:28,097
What in the actual hell is it
going on about all of a sudden?

128
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:30,197
I think it seeks to prove
that human beings are

129
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,817
not the only ones capable
of having intellect.

130
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:34,817
Even planktons like it can make memories.

131
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,400
I said my name is FF!

132
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:37,417
Didn't you hear me?

133
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:40,618
It's painfully obvious I'm
more intelligent than you!

134
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:42,210
Not good.

135
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:45,537
It's going to hide the disks somewhere
new before we can get to them!

136
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:49,385
If it manages to bury them
underground, they'll be gone forever!

137
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:53,160
J-Jolene, there's something else.

138
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,220
Look behind us!

139
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:57,537
The one that attacked us in
the water earlier is back,

140
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:59,620
and it's trying to grab the guard.

141
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:01,756
Shit, the handcuffs!

142
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:04,687
If we get 50 meters away
from it, we're dead!

143
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:06,658
We're done, Jolene.

144
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,820
It's time to give up on the discs.

145
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:11,117
Our priority should be
protecting the guard's body?

146
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:15,671
Before we get blown up, because I'd
rather make it out of this in one piece.

147
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:19,177
You're right, but I'll let
you handle the handcuffs.

148
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:20,090
Hermes.

149
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:24,757
While I'm running to the storehouse,

150
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:27,917
it's up to you to protect the guard
and haul his body within my safety

151
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,337
range so my cop doesn't go off
and blow me up before I get there.

152
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:32,250
Got no choice.

153
00:08:32,333 --> 00:08:33,454
Hey, hold on a second.

154
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:36,740
What a crazy bitch. That's ridiculous.

155
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:40,182
Why would she leave
something like that up to me?

156
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,180
But still, goddammit.

157
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:46,297
Once it pulls the guard's
body into the water,

158
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:49,733
both Jolene and I are going
to get blown to kingdom come.

159
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:53,700
I have no time to waste!

160
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:07,980
Hell yeah, I managed to do it.

161
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:11,691
But one thing's for sure,

162
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:15,557
after this bullshit, I ain't ever going
to use my stickers like this again.

163
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:19,111
I can't believe I actually had
to double my arm to do this.

164
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:23,620
Aw, man, I bet it's
gonna hurt like a bitch.

165
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:32,740
Now I just need to carry in within
50 meters of that stupid storehouse.

166
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:36,470
Water?

167
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:44,040
Damn you, you filthy little maggot!

168
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,611
That's a victory, Scream.

169
00:09:57,760 --> 00:10:00,231
You think you've won, don't you, shithead?

170
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:03,920
Take a good look.

171
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:05,577
This is the corpse of that poor girl with

172
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:07,937
the undercut that your
other half sucked dry.

173
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:09,660
She's got no moisture left.

174
00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:13,337
And now, thanks to my sticker,
she's been divided into two.

175
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:15,280
All I gotta do is pull it off.

176
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:25,917
That ought to absorb whatever
water is left over like a maxi pad.

177
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,765
Or should I say it'll dry up like
a drop of water in the desert.

178
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,220
Put a sock in it!

179
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,377
You're in my way!

180
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:34,720
Get lost, would ya?

181
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:45,100
Jolene, the only way we'll
win is if we dry it out.

182
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,868
In order to defeat that
disgusting parasite,

183
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:52,139
we've got to drain its tank
like it did those girls.

184
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:10,580
You actually made it.

185
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:12,517
I was going to kill you anyway.

186
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:14,188
You've just made it easier.

187
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:17,397
My original plan was to hide the discs

188
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:19,917
somewhere else and then
ask you some questions,

189
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:20,830
but no matter.

190
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:23,020
For now, answer me this.

191
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:29,786
Are you going to step into this puddle
I've made, or will you run for your life?

192
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,802
Which way would you like to die?

193
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:37,417
If we're asking questions,
I've got some too.

194
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:40,029
Do you know who the
one behind all this is?

195
00:11:40,540 --> 00:11:42,197
Who exactly is Pale Snake?

196
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:47,620
Also, by gathering all the disks together,
what are they really hoping to achieve?

197
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:49,717
My, you're an interesting one.

198
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:53,357
I can understand the motive behind
fighting to protect yourself.

199
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:55,852
Or even fighting to protect your friends.

200
00:11:55,980 --> 00:12:00,333
Well, that's not something I can relate
to, but I can see why you'd do it.

201
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:05,351
However, what I don't understand is why
you'd willingly walk in here to die.

202
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:11,462
Also, as for the one known as Pale Snake,
unfortunately, I don't know who they are.

203
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:19,801
Did you think I was
distracted, you moronic child?

204
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:25,620
The entirety of this puddle has
already become a part of my body!

205
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:34,157
Were you trying to soak
up the water with flour?

206
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:36,457
I commend your effort, but you failed.

207
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:37,740
Well, it was futile.

208
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:40,197
I have full understanding
of my power and created

209
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:43,398
an environment for myself
where I have no weaknesses.

210
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:46,820
Your body seems to be a worthy vessel.

211
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:50,374
Perhaps I can live inside of
it comfortably for a while.

212
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:53,100
Nah, because now you've already lost.

213
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:56,877
When you made this so-called
perfect environment for yourself,

214
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:59,607
